Description: CVE-2026-14679 - Fix stack buffer overflow in argument name matching
 Stack buffer overflow in PostgreSQL argument name matching allows an object
 creator to write 0x0 and 0x1 bytes past a FUNC_MAX_ARGS-sized stack array
 via OUT parameter count. Replace the too-short arggiven[] array with a
 palloc'd one, enforce FUNC_MAX_ARGS-1 for aggregates, and replace PL/Tcl's
 fixed argument-name buffer with a Tcl_DString.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/postgres/postgres/commit/cf44ff5e66353264451ac239b39e9053e8d138e6
Author: Tom Lane <tgl@sss.pgh.pa.us>
Last-Update: 2026-08-21

