Description: CVE-2026-14662 - Harden tsvector and tsquery code against integer overflows
 Backport of two upstream fixes (CWE-190) for text-search overflow bugs:
 .
 tsvector hardening (commit 7c2ba321d35f18f2c5dc7b5c4a212467f7fb2fc5):
  * make_tsvector()/parsetext() now reject lexemes whose length is <= 0 or
    exceeds MAXSTRLEN, and enforce the MAXSTRPOS total-length limit, so
    array_to_tsvector() and to_tsvector() cannot build invalid tsvectors.
  * array_to_tsvector() additionally rejects empty and over-length lexemes
    and enforces MAXSTRPOS on the total data length.
  * tsvectorrecv() rejects empty-string lexemes and enforces MAXSTRPOS on the
    accumulated lexeme data, matching the other tsvector constructors.
  * tsvectorout() sizes its output buffer with a size_t accumulator and drops
    the bogus pg_database_encoding_max_length() multiplier, fixing an output
    buffer sizing bug.
  * Length accumulators widened to size_t and error messages standardized to
    the %zu format.
 .
 tsquery hardening (commit 1e3014f373c77c2bdd52766b5c14c7ea2653b838):
  * QTN2QT()/cntsize() widen their sumlen/nnode counters from int to size_t to
    avoid under-allocation and heap overwrite on large tree expansions.
  * fillQT() validates that each operand distance fits the 20-bit qoperand
    field (MAXSTRPOS) before storing it.
  * TSQUERY_TOO_BIG() adds an explicit overflow guard on lenofoperand.
 .
 The two tsvector.c/tsvector_op.c hunks were hand-adapted to REL_13_STABLE's
 code (PG14-only refactors around pg_mblen_range and parse_weight are absent in
 PG13); the net behavior is identical to upstream.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/postgres/postgres/commit/7c2ba321d35f18f2c5dc7b5c4a212467f7fb2fc5
