Description: CVE-2026-14670 - Harden PL/Perl code against "tied" Perl arrays and hashes
 Heap buffer overflow in plperl: a function owner can execute arbitrary code
 as the OS user running the database via a crafted function body that returns
 a "tied" Perl array or hash.
 .
 Tied arrays may report a different size each time they are inspected, so
 plperl_array_to_datum()'s helper read av_len() once per level for the loop
 bound and again for the recorded dimension. If the array shrank in between,
 fewer elements were accumulated than the dimensions claimed and
 makeMdArrayResult() read past the accumulated data, producing a corrupt
 result array. array_to_datum_internal() now takes its loop bound from the
 already-recorded dims[cur_depth - 1] so the built array and the reported
 dimensions can never disagree; missing entries become NULLs and extra ones
 are ignored.
 .
 plperl_to_hstore() sized its Pairs array from hv_iterinit()'s return value,
 which per the Perl documentation "is currently only meaningful for hashes
 without tie magic". A tied hash could under-report its size and the
 hv_iternext() loop would then write past the end of the allocation. The
 allocation now starts at an arbitrary guess and is grown on demand, and the
 actual number of pairs collected is passed to hstoreUniquePairs() instead of
 the untrusted count.
 .
 Backport notes for postgresql-13 13.23-0+deb11u4: upstream scoped this fix
 "Backpatch-through: 14" only because PostgreSQL 13 is EOL, not because 13 is
 unaffected -- both vulnerable functions are present and structurally
 identical in 13.23, so the fix is applied unchanged apart from one
 reconciliation. Upstream's hunk also converts the Pairs allocation to
 palloc_array(); Debian's own quilt patch
 0051-Use-palloc_array-in-a-few-more-places-to-avoid-overf.patch has already
 made that conversion in this tree, so the allocation line is left as
 pre-existing context here and only the count handling changes.
 repalloc_array() is available and is overflow-checked in this tree via
 Debian's 0041-Make-palloc_array-and-friends-safe-against-integer-o.patch.
 The unrelated CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS() and "!value ||" changes visible in
 upstream's REL_14_STABLE copy of hstore_plperl.c belong to other commits and
 are deliberately not included.
