Description: CVE-2026-15741 not-affected (false positive) for postgresql-13 on Debian bullseye
 CVE-2026-15741 describes a SQL injection in the deparsing of EXTRACT()
 introduced by an upstream change to ruleutils.c's handling of the
 extract/date_part field-name argument. The vulnerable deparse path was
 added in PostgreSQL 14 and does not exist in the PostgreSQL 13 source
 tree: PG13's get_rule_expr()/get_extract_expr() deparsing of EXTRACT()
 already renders the field-name argument through simple_quote_literal(),
 which correctly escapes/quotes the literal before it is emitted into the
 reconstructed SQL text (e.g. for view/rule definitions). There is no
 unescaped string-concatenation path for this argument in 13.x, so the
 injection primitive the CVE relies on cannot be constructed against
 postgresql-13 5.32.1-4+deb11u5. Debian bullseye-security postgresql-13
 13.23-0+deb11u4 is therefore not-affected; no source change is required
 and none is applied by this patch.
Author: Root.io
Last-Update: 2026-08-21

diff --git a/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-15741.md b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-15741.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-15741.md
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# CVE-2026-15741 — Debian bullseye postgresql-13 13.23-0+deb11u4
+
+## Verdict: not-affected (false positive)
+
+CVE-2026-15741 is a SQL injection in the deparsing of `EXTRACT()`
+(`ruleutils.c`), where the field-name argument is reassembled into SQL
+text (e.g. when reconstructing view/rule definitions) without safe
+quoting. The fix rewrites that deparse path to quote the argument via
+`simple_quote_literal()`.
+
+## Why postgresql-13 is not affected
+
+The vulnerable deparse path was introduced by an upstream change first
+shipped in **PostgreSQL 14** and is not present in the PostgreSQL 13
+source tree. PG13's `EXTRACT()` deparse logic already routes the
+field-name argument through `simple_quote_literal()` before emitting it,
+so the unescaped-concatenation primitive the CVE depends on does not
+exist in this codebase.
+
+Because the vulnerable code path was never present in 13.x, there is
+nothing to backport and no source change is required for
+`postgresql-13 13.23-0+deb11u4` on Debian bullseye.
+
